 Michigan for the first time since 2014 with a 20-14 victory.","published":"2026-10-03T21:23:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50092593/minnesota-outlasts-michigan-struggling-qb-bryce-underwood","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Minnesota QB Lindsey arrested after alcohol, fake ID accusations","description":"Minnesota starting quarterback Drake Lindsey, 20, was arrested early Friday in Arkansas and accused of underage alcohol possession and possession of a fake ID.","published":"2026-05-01T21:14:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/48648720/minnesota-qb-lindsey-arrested-underage-alcohol-fake-id","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College Football Playoff top 12 projection after Week 11","description":"We assess how the selection committee could stack the top teams in the country after Week 11.","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480953/projecting-2026-playoff-top-12-week-11-cfp","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"No. 2 Utah survives, stays unbeaten on late 70-yard TD in thriller vs. Arizona","description":"In a back-and-forth thriller, Utah rallied to remain undefeated after Devon Dampier hit Creed Whittemore on a 70-yard score late in a 40-39 win over Arizona.","published":"2026-11-15T14:23:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488650/no-2-utah-survives-late-70-yard-td-thriller-vs-arizona","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Patience starting to run thin for head coaches in Week 11","description":"Saturday didn't offer much to change the season's complexion, but some coaches are coming under pressure.","published":"2026-11-15T08:17:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedayfinal111426/week-11-top-games-highlights-takeaways","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Predicting the College Football Playoff: Who's most likely to make the field?","description":"Find out which teams our experts think will make this season's CFP.","published":"2026-11-15T07:48:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions111426/cfp-predictions-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Kiffin understands frustration as LSU's playoff hopes dashed","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin said it was fair to question the team's 6-4 record this season after losing to Texas on Saturday, a defeat that likely knocked LSU out of playoff contention.","published":"2026-11-15T08:55:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488081/kiffin-understands-frustration-lsu-playoff-hopes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest's post-blowout jab at SMU tops college football Week 11 trolls","description":"Wake Forest dominated SMU on the gridiron Saturday -- and added insult to injury after the game.","published":"2026-11-15T05:30:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5144959/drake-lindsey","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_Lindsey"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Drake Lindsey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_Lindsey","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:54Z","intro":"Drake Lindsey (born August 18, 2005) is an American college football quarterback for the Minnesota Golden Gophers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lindsey attended Fayetteville High School in Fayetteville, Arkansas. As a junior, he threw for 3,778 yards, 37 touchdowns and three interceptions in 11 games, and was named the 2023 Arkansas MaxPreps Player of the Year. As a senior, Lindsey threw for 3,916 yards and 52 touchdowns, while completing 69.6% of his pass attempts, and was named the 2024 Arkansas Gatorade Player of the Year. Coming out of high school, he was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Minnesota Golden Gophers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman in 2024, Lindsey completed four of five pass attempts for 50 yards and a touchdown in three games. Ahead of the 2025 season, he entered a quarterback competition with Dylan Wittke, Max Shikenjanski, and Jackson Kollock.\nLindsey completed the 2025 regular season starting every game for the University of Minnesota. He finished with 2,235 passing yards, 16 touchdowns, and six interceptions. He led the Gophers to a record of 7-5 (5-4 in the Big Ten), and won his first career start vs Minnesota's biggest rival, the University of Wisconsin."}]}}